  "aiContextParagraph": "The Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) and the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) have officially reconciled, ending a six-year split to form a coalition for the upcoming Punjab assembly elections. This political development has drawn sharp criticism from opposition members within the Punjab Congress. Party leadership has publicly questioned the effectiveness of the alliance, suggesting that voter resentment stemming from past issues, such as the farmers' protest, persists. Furthermore, concerns have been raised regarding the impact of this political shift on regional law and order. While the reunion has brought both parties back into electoral contention, the opposition has characterized the move as struggling to overcome significant past fractures. Discussions regarding the strategic implications of this partnership continue as both parties prepare their joint campaign strategies for the 2027 state elections.",
